VALUES ('frederick.stone@harmonygames.co/<CAPBs_a398e8c9d40f2711c7bb28205e03c80601741499a@mail.gmail.com>', 'frederick.stone@harmonygames.co/1844639871009298010', 'frederick.stone@harmonygames.co', '["INBOX", "CATEGORY_PERSONAL"]', 'Fred - this is the category list Griffin wants from Q3. -L ---------- Forwarded message --------- From: PERSON_2847_NAME <PERSON_2847_EMAIL>', 1759185668000, '2025-09-29T22:41:08Z', 2515, 'Fwd: Q2 metrics - opex categories', 'leonard.hayes@harmonygames.co', 'Leonard Hayes', '["Frederick Stone <frederick.stone@harmonygames.co>"]', '[]', '[]', '[]', E'Fred - this is the category list Griffin wants from Q3. -L\r\n\r\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\r\nFrom: PERSON_2847_NAME <PERSON_2847_EMAIL>\r\nDate: Tue, Aug 12, 2025 at 10:31 AM\r\nSubject: Q2 metrics - opex categories\r\nTo: Leonard Hayes <leonard.hayes@harmonygames.co>\r\n\r\nHi Leonard,\r\n\r\nThanks for getting Q2 in. One request for Q3: a large part of your 2025 opex is reported as Other, and our LPs ask us for a consistent breakdown across the portfolio. From the Q3 submission please report non-payroll opex in our 2025 categories:\r\n\r\nSoftware & subscriptions: all SaaS and app subscriptions, whichever team uses them, including AI tools, design and stock libraries, market-intelligence tools, e-signature, e-mail and scheduling tools, automation tools and app store developer program fees.\r\nHosting & infrastructure: cloud, backend-as-a-service, domains, and website builders and hosting.\r\nResearch & user testing: paid playtests, surveys and research panels.\r\nMarketing (non-UA): creative production and freelancers for marketing assets (store screenshots, trailers).\r\nTravel & events: flights, hotels, ground transport and conference passes.\r\nHardware & equipment: devices, test hardware and accessories, including retail purchases of them.\r\nProfessional & admin: legal and accounting, payroll, HR, equity and accounting platforms, registered agent, federal and state filings and fees.\r\nOther G&A: bank fees not tied to a purchase, shipping, coworking and office, and team meals.\r\n\r\nPaid user acquisition is reported separately and should not be in opex. Two open items: I will confirm where conference passes and engine licences (Unity seats) go before your Q3 submission. These replace the 2024 list.\r\n\r\nBest,\r\nPERSON_2847_NAME', NULL, '[{"name": "Message-ID", "value": "<CAPBs_a398e8c9d40f2711c7bb28205e03c80601741499a@mail.gmail.com>"}, {"name": "Date", "value": "Mon, 29 Sep 2025 22:41:08 +0000"}, {"name": "Subject", "value": "Fwd: Q2 metrics - opex categories"}, {"name": "From", "value": "Leonard Hayes <leonard.hayes@harmonygames.co>"}, {"name": "To", "value": "Frederick Stone <frederick.stone@harmonygames.co>"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[]');
